-- title:
--   Branches through an ∞-chart cusp lie over the Γ₀(qM') Gauss ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero and algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$; let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of the $f$ with $f \cdot y = x$ for power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction. On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}$ of $K$ over $A$ (the pushout of the spectra of the algebras of elements integral over $A[j]$, resp. over $A[j^{-1}]$), let $z$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism $\mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\infty$-chart algebra mapping to $z$, with $\mathfrak{p}_y$ maximal, containing $j^{-1}$, and containing every element of the $\infty$-chart algebra that is a non-unit of $W_0$. Let $K_0 \subseteq K_0' \subseteq K$ be the $L$-subfields generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function fields of $\Gamma_0(M')$ and of $\Gamma_0(qM')$, with valuation subrings $O_0$, $O_0'$ defined by the same power-series-ratio condition. Then, for the algebra structures given by the inclusions, every valuation subring $B$ of $K$ such that $x \in O_0 \iff x \in B$ for all $x \in K_0$, and such that every element of the $\infty$-chart algebra that is a non-unit of $B$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}_y$, satisfies $x \in O_0' \iff x \in B$ for all $x \in K_0'$.
--
--   This is the cusp-side counterpart, on the pole ($j^{-1}$) chart, of the statement that a branch of $K$ through a given point of the special fibre which lies over the Gauss ring of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor must already lie over the chosen Gauss ring of the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-floor: the two branches of $\Gamma_0(qM')$ over $\Gamma_0(M')$ in the special fibre meet only at supersingular points, never at cusps. It is used in the proof that the relevant height-one valuations of $K$ are unramified over the base at such points, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_of_height_one_of_algebraMap_mem_chartAlgInf_of_jInvChartInf_mem_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_of_height_one_of_algebraMap_mem_chartAlgInf_of_jInvChartInf_mem_xH).
